---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Timeline from '../components/Timeline.astro';
import { contact, experience, education, skills, fmt } from '../data/profile';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
---

<Base
  title="Experience · Motto Sereeyothin"
  description="Work experience, education, projects and skills of Weerapraj (Motto) Sereeyothin."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Experience</p>
    <h2 class="page-title">Work, education, and the things I’ve built</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      A closer look at where I’ve worked, what I studied, and the tools I reach for.
    </p>
    <p><a class="button" href={contact.resume} download="Weerapraj-Sereeyothin-Resume.pdf">Download resume (PDF)</a></p>
  </header>

  <section class="prose">
    <p>
      Most of my experience comes from Northeastern’s co-op program and from student organizations, which together
      gave me a mix of full-time industry work and part-time campus projects. I started in the summer of 2023 as a
      software development intern at ECARTSTUDIO in Bangkok. There I helped build a high-traffic
      React and TypeScript web app for a Thai municipality, which taught me how much a clear interface matters when
      thousands of residents depend on it to reach public services.
    </p>
    <p>
      Back in Boston, I joined Northeastern Electric Racing as a software developer and worked on
      the project management software the 200+ member team uses to coordinate building a race car. My first co-op,
      at GhostLab, focused on data. I designed an interactive analytics dashboard that lets
      engineering professors track student progress, spot trends early, and give targeted support. I then
      helped the Student Government Association modernize its senate application and nomination
      process, and spent the second half of 2025 as a software engineer co-op at Spill Center.
    </p>
    <p>
      Across these roles, I’ve worked mostly on the front end and on the APIs that feed it, and I care about
      shipping things that are fast, accessible, and easy for the next developer to pick up. The timeline below shows
      how my education and work overlap. Hover over or tab to any bar for details.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Timeline entries={[...experience, ...education]} />

  <section class="split">
    <div>
      <h3>Experience</h3>
      <ol class="entries">
        {
          experience.map((e) => (
            <li class="entry">
              <div class="entry-meta">
                <span class="entry-dates">{fmt(e.start)} – {fmt(e.end)}</span>
                <span class="entry-loc">{e.location}</span>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h4>{e.title}</h4>
                <p class="entry-org">{e.org}</p>
                {e.summary && <p>{e.summary}</p>}
                {e.skills && (
                  <ul class="tags" aria-label="Skills">
                    {e.skills.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}
                  </ul>
                )}
              </div>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>

    <aside>
      <h3>Education</h3>
      <ul class="plain-list">
        {
          education.map((e) => (
            <li>
              <strong>{e.org}</strong>
              <span>{e.title}</span>
              <span class="entry-dates">{fmt(e.start)} – {fmt(e.end)}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>

      <h3>Project</h3>
      <div class="project">
        <strong>ScheduleNEU</strong>
        <span class="entry-dates">Dec 2023 – Present</span>
        <p>
          A schedule-planning website for Northeastern students, built by parsing data from Northeastern’s class
          catalog.
        </p>
        <a class="project-shot" href="https://www.scheduleneu.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <img
            src={`${base}images/scheduleneu.jpg`}
            width="1200"
            height="633"
            loading="lazy"
            alt="ScheduleNEU homepage with the tagline “Simplify, Plan, Achieve” and a husky peeking over a calendar"
          />
        </a>
        <a href="https://www.scheduleneu.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit scheduleneu.com →</a>
      </div>

      <h3>Skills</h3>
      <ul class="tags">
        {skills.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </aside>
  </section>
</Base>
